Overrated;
Some will like it, but as someone who worked their way through titles such as Thief 2 as Deus Ex, I found that this was a glossier, shallower impersonation.
A number of things killed it for me;
The fact that ultimately, it doesn't really matter what you do. It purports to be a stealth game but the stealth is sort of faked - after a patient, methodical doing away of guards without killing them I was met with a respawn. As opposed to the more realistic use of shadow and guard AI in Thief 2 here you can evade detection from guards simply by not being at eye level.
On the other hand, if you run around like a maniac, stabbing and using your blink ability, you can clear levels in a matter of minutes.
The Outsider is a sort of late 2000s emo rock who provides you with your narcissistic supply and assorted superhero powers, in the guise of a dickensian assassin.

